{"cuisine/maasai-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/maasai-cuisine","n":"Maasai cuisine","c":"#e46a3f","crumb":[["Africa","cuisines#africa"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Kenya","intro":[["The Maasai () are an Eastern Nilotic ethnic group native to northern, central and southern regions of Kenya including northern Tanzania, near the African Great Lakes region. Their native language is Maa, a Nilotic language related to Dinka, Kalenjin and Nuer, a branch within the broader Nilo-Saharan language family. Except for some elders living in rural areas, most Maasai people speak the official languages of Kenya and Tanzania—Swahili and English."],["The Maasai population has been reported as numbering 1,189,522 in Kenya in the 2019 census compared to 377,089 in the 1989 census."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"maasai-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maasai_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[]}],"cont":"African cuisine","img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/f/f1/Bodymodmassai.jpg","w":500,"h":749,"by":"http://www.dmitrimarkine.com","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bodymodmassai.jpg"}},"cuisine/kaiseki":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/kaiseki","n":"Kaiseki","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Japan","intro":[["Kaiseki or kaiseki-ryōri (懐石料理) is a traditional multi-course Japanese dinner. The term also refers to the collection of skills and techniques that allow the preparation of such meals and is analogous to Western haute cuisine."],["There are two kinds of traditional Japanese meal styles called kaiseki or kaiseki-ryōri. The first, where kaiseki is written as \"会席\" and kaiseki-ryōri as \"会席料理\", refers to a set menu of select food served on an individual tray (to each member of a gathering). The second, written as \"懐石\" and as \"懐石料理\", refers to the simple meal that the host of a chanoyu gathering serves to the guests before a ceremonial tea, and is also known as cha-kaiseki (茶懐石). The development of nouvelle cuisine was likely inspired by kaiseki principles."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"kaiseki"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaiseki"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Kaiseki: The Exquisite Cuisine of Kyoto's Kikunoi Restaurant","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Yoshihiro Murata, 2006","note":"Seasonal kaiseki menus from the chef of Kyoto's Kikunoi, published by Kodansha.","url":"https://penguinrandomhouse.com/books/563552/kaiseki-by-yoshihiro-murata-foreword-by-ferran-adria-foreword-by-nobu-matsuhisa-photographs-by-masashi-kuma","suggested":true,"isbn":"9781568364421"}]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/6/69/Jisaku_Kaiseki_Ryori_01.jpg/500px-Jisaku_Kaiseki_Ryori_01.jpg","w":500,"h":290,"by":"Chris 73 / Wikimedia Commons","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jisaku_Kaiseki_Ryori_01.jpg"}},"cuisine/bangladeshi-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/bangladeshi-cuisine","n":"Bangladeshi cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Bangladesh","intro":[["Bangladeshi cuisine has been shaped by the region's history and riverine geography. Bangladesh has a tropical monsoon climate. The staple foods of Bangladesh are rice and fish. The majority of Bangladeshi people are ethnic Bengali, with a minority of non-Bengalis, many of whom are used to cuisines from different traditions and regions."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"bangladeshi-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bangladeshi_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":6,"links":[["Chhanamukhi","dish/chhanamukhi"],["Durus kura","dish/durus-kura"],["Shemai","dish/shemai"],["Shorshe ilish","dish/shorshe-ilish"],["Thali","dish/thali"],["Zarda (food)","dish/zarda-food"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Made in Bangladesh: Recipes and Stories from a Home Kitchen","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Dina Begum","note":"Bangladeshi home cooking by a London-based food writer, published by Hardie Grant.","url":"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/9781784886523","suggested":true,"isbn":"9781784886523"}]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Cardamom","ingredient/cardamom"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Chhena","ingredient/chhena"],["Maida (flour)","ingredient/maida-flour"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Cashew nut","ingredient/cashew-nut"],["Ghee","ingredient/ghee"],["Vermicelli","ingredient/vermicelli"],["Hilsa","ingredient/hilsa"],["Ilish","ingredient/ilish"],["Mustard","ingredient/mustard"],["Mustard (condiment)","ingredient/mustard-condiment"],["Mustard oil","ingredient/mustard-oil"],["Turmeric","ingredient/turmeric"],["Groat","ingredient/groat"],["Almond","ingredient/almond"],["Pistachio","ingredient/pistachio"],["Raisin","ingredient/raisin"],["Saffron","ingredient/saffron"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Within Bangladeshi cooking","count":1,"links":[["Bengali cuisine","cuisine/bengali-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/4/4a/Hilsha_fish_curry.jpg/500px-Hilsha_fish_curry.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Ferdous","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hilsha_fish_curry.jpg"}},"cuisine/macedonian-cuisine-greek":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/macedonian-cuisine-greek","n":"Macedonian cuisine (Greek)","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["Greek cuisine","cuisine/greek-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Greece","intro":[["The cusinine of Greek Macedonia is the cuisine of the region of Macedonia in Greece. Contemporary Greek Macedonian cooking shares much with general Greek, wider Balkan and Mediterranean cuisine, and inherits from Ottoman cuisine. From all the communities that have settled in the region main specific gastronomic influences include dishes of the Asia Minor Greek, Aromanian and Megleno-Romanian, Pontic Greek, Slavic, Armenian and Sephardi Jewish populations."],["Contemporary Greek-Macedonian cuisine has developed in recent years, with several food companies and restaurants receiving distinctions."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"macedonian-cuisine-greek"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macedonian_cuisine_(Greek)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Greek cuisine","cuisine/greek-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Greek cuisine","cuisine/greek-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"European cuisine","img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/5/5f/Greek_Salad_Choriatiki.jpg/500px-Greek_Salad_Choriatiki.jpg","w":500,"h":381,"by":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/zone41/","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greek_Salad_Choriatiki.jpg"}},"cuisine/english-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/english-cuisine","n":"English cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in United Kingdom","intro":[["English cuisine encompasses the cooking styles, traditions and recipes associated with England. It has distinctive attributes of its own, but is also very similar to wider British cuisine, partly historically and partly due to the import of ingredients and ideas from the Americas, China, and India during the time of the British Empire and as a result of post-war immigration."],["Some traditional meals, such as bread and cheese, roasted and stewed meats, meat and game pies, boiled vegetables and broths with herbs or spices, and freshwater and saltwater fish have ancient origins. The 14th-century English cookbook, the Forme of Cury, contains recipes for these, and dates from the royal court of Richard II."],["English cooking has been influenced by foreign ingredients and cooking styles since the Middle Ages. Curry was introduced from the Indian subcontinent and adapted to English tastes from the eighteenth century with Hannah Glasse's recipe for chicken \"currey\". French cuisine influenced English recipes throughout the Victorian era. After the rationing of the Second World War, Elizabeth David's 1950 A Book of Mediterranean Food had wide influence, bringing the cuisines of that region, including of Italy, to English homes. Her success encouraged other cookery writers to describe other styles, including Chinese and Thai cuisine. England continues to absorb culinary ideas from all over the world."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"english-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":13,"links":[["Angels on horseback","dish/angels-on-horseback"],["Cabinet pudding","dish/cabinet-pudding"],["Clotted cream","dish/clotted-cream"],["Crème anglaise","dish/creme-anglaise"],["Fish and chips","dish/fish-and-chips"],["Macaroni and cheese","dish/macaroni-and-cheese"],["Maids of honour tart","dish/maids-of-honour-tart"],["Manchester tart","dish/manchester-tart"],["Mock turtle soup","dish/mock-turtle-soup"],["Pie and mash","dish/pie-and-mash"],["Pork pie","dish/pork-pie"],["Pottage","dish/pottage"],["Windsor soup","dish/windsor-soup"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"English Food","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Jane Grigson, 1974","note":"Classic collection of traditional English recipes with historical notes.","url":"https://www.penguin.co.uk/books/24292/english-food-by-jane-grigson-revised-by-sophie-grigsonilustrated-by-gillian-zeiner-with-a-further-selection-by-clare-leighton-and-eric-ravilious/9780140273243","suggested":true,"isbn":"9780140273243"}]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Fish","ingredient/fish"],["Shortcrust pastry","ingredient/shortcrust-pastry"],["Bacon","ingredient/bacon"],["Oyster","ingredient/oyster"],["Sponge cake","ingredient/sponge-cake"],["Egg yolk","ingredient/egg-yolk"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Vanilla","ingredient/vanilla"],["Atlantic cod","ingredient/atlantic-cod"],["French fries","ingredient/french-fries"],["Fried fish","ingredient/fried-fish"],["Fries","ingredient/fries"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Cheddar cheese","ingredient/cheddar-cheese"],["Cheddar sauce","ingredient/cheddar-sauce"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Macaroni","ingredient/macaroni"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Cheese curds","ingredient/cheese-curds"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Puff pastry","ingredient/puff-pastry"],["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Within English cooking","count":3,"links":[["Cornish cuisine","cuisine/cornish-cuisine"],["Devonian cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-devon"],["Dorset cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-dorset"]]}],"cont":"European cuisine","img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/3/3c/Tea_at_the_Rittenhouse_Hotel.jpg/500px-Tea_at_the_Rittenhouse_Hotel.jpg","w":500,"h":625,"by":"joyosity","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tea_at_the_Rittenhouse_Hotel.jpg"}},"ingredient/paprika":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/paprika","n":"Paprika","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 15 dishes across 16 cuisines","intro":[["Paprika is a spice made from dried and ground red peppers, Capsicum annuum. It is traditionally made from Capsicum annuum varietals in the Longum group, and while it can have varying levels of heat, the peppers used tend to be milder and have thinner flesh than those used to produce chili powder. The milder, sweet paprika is mainly composed of the fruit of the pepper with most of the seeds removed; whereas some seeds and stalks are retained in the peppers used for hotter paprika."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-paprika"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paprika"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":16,"groups":[["Hungarian cuisine","cuisine/hungarian-cuisine",[["Chicken paprikash","dish/chicken-paprikash"],["Goulash","dish/goulash"],["Gulyásleves","dish/gulyasleves"],["Lecsó","dish/lecso"],["Pörkölt","dish/porkolt"]]],["Austrian cuisine","cuisine/austrian-cuisine",[["Chicken paprikash","dish/chicken-paprikash"],["Gulyásleves","dish/gulyasleves"]]],["Galician cuisine","cuisine/galician-cuisine",[["Androlla","dish/androlla"],["Polbo á feira","dish/polbo-a-feira"]]],["Arab cuisine","cuisine/arab-cuisine",[["Shawarma","dish/shawarma"]]],["Aragonese cuisine","cuisine/aragonese-cuisine",[["Chistorra","dish/chistorra"]]],["Bolivian cuisine","cuisine/bolivian-cuisine",[["Locro","dish/locro"]]],["Bulgarian cuisine","cuisine/bulgarian-cuisine",[["Lyutenitsa","dish/lyutenitsa"]]],["Ecuadorian cuisine","cuisine/ecuadorian-cuisine",[["Locro","dish/locro"]]],["Georgian cuisine","cuisine/georgian-cuisine",[["Ajika","dish/ajika"]]],["Moroccan cuisine","cuisine/moroccan-cuisine",[["Taktouka","dish/taktouka"]]],["Peruvian cuisine","cuisine/peruvian-cuisine",[["Locro","dish/locro"]]],["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine",[["Goulash","dish/goulash"]]],["Spanish cuisine","cuisine/spanish-cuisine",[["Chistorra","dish/chistorra"]]],["Thai cuisine","cuisine/thai-cuisine",[["Boat noodles","dish/boat-noodles"]]],["Turkish cuisine","cuisine/turkish-cuisine",[["Düğün çorbası","dish/dugun-corbas"]]],["Viennese cuisine","cuisine/viennese-cuisine",[["Goulash","dish/goulash"]]]]},{"h":"Where it's grown","grown":{"what":"Chillies and peppers, dry (Capsicum spp., Pimenta spp.), raw","years":"2020 to 2024","url":"https://www.fao.org/faostat/en/#data/QCL","world":4829669,"top":[["India","cuisine/indian-cuisine",2289969],["China","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",325652],["Thailand","cuisine/thai-cuisine",322854],["Bangladesh","cuisine/bangladeshi-cuisine",319906],["Ethiopia","cuisine/ethiopian-cuisine",274388],["Myanmar","cuisine/burmese-cuisine",143674],["Côte d'Ivoire","cuisine/ivorian-cuisine",131639],["Pakistan","cuisine/pakistani-cuisine",124273],["Ghana","cuisine/ghanaian-cuisine",110991],["Vietnam","cuisine/vietnamese-cuisine",100062],["Nepal","cuisine/nepalese-cuisine",74501],["Nigeria","cuisine/nigerian-cuisine",64464],["Egypt","cuisine/egyptian-cuisine",62902],["Mexico","cuisine/mexican-cuisine",61146],["Cameroon","cuisine/cameroonian-cuisine",42913]]}},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Cinnamon","ingredient/cinnamon"],["Parsley","ingredient/parsley"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Coriander","ingredient/coriander"],["Herbs","ingredient/herbs"],["Khmeli suneli","ingredient/khmeli-suneli"],["Vinegar","ingredient/vinegar"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/8/81/Piment%C3%B3n_Tap_de_Cort%C3%AD_%28cropped%29.jpg","w":500,"h":281,"by":"Marcosgarrido88","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Piment%C3%B3n_Tap_de_Cort%C3%AD_(cropped).jpg"}},"dish/angel-food-cake":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/angel-food-cake","n":"Angel food cake","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Angel food cake or angel cake is a type of sponge cake made with egg whites, sugar, and flour, and without oil, baking powder, and various other ingredients common in cakes. It is made in a process of whipping egg whites to a foam, beating in sugar, and folding in flour and more sugar. After baking in a pan with a tube in its center, the cake is hung upside down until cool. The final cake has a slightly chewy texture and white interior."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-angel-food-cake"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angel_food_cake"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Cream of tartar","ingredient/cream-of-tartar"],["Egg white","ingredient/egg-white"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"More from American cuisine","links":[["Banana bread","dish/banana-bread"],["Banana pudding","dish/banana-pudding"],["Barbecue sauce","dish/barbecue-sauce"],["Beer cake","dish/beer-cake"],["Better than sex cake","dish/better-than-sex-cake"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Blooming onion","dish/blooming-onion"],["Brown Betty (dessert)","dish/brown-betty-dessert"],["Brunswick stew","dish/brunswick-stew"],["Buffalo wing","dish/buffalo-wing"],["Butter cake","dish/butter-cake"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Caramel apple","dish/caramel-apple"],["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Cheesesteak","dish/cheesesteak"],["Chicago-style hot dog","dish/chicago-style-hot-dog"],["Chicken nugget","dish/chicken-nugget"],["Chiffon cake","dish/chiffon-cake"],["Chili con carne","dish/chili-con-carne"],["Chimichanga","dish/chimichanga"],["Chow-chow (food)","dish/chow-chow-food"],["Chowder","dish/chowder"],["Cioppino","dish/cioppino"],["Clam chowder","dish/clam-chowder"],["Clam dip","dish/clam-dip"],["Club sandwich","dish/club-sandwich"],["Cobb salad","dish/cobb-salad"],["Cobbler (food)","dish/cobbler-food"],["Cook's Corner","dish/cook-s-corner"],["Crab cake","dish/crab-cake"],["Croffle","dish/croffle"],["Dagwood Bumstead","dish/dagwood-bumstead"],["Dagwood sandwich","dish/dagwood-sandwich"],["Deep-dish pizza","dish/deep-dish-pizza"],["Desperation pie","dish/desperation-pie"],["Dirty rice","dish/dirty-rice"],["Donut hole","dish/donut-hole"],["Egg in the basket","dish/egg-in-the-basket"],["Fish and chips","dish/fish-and-chips"],["Fritter","dish/fritter"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/6/64/AngelFoodCake.jpg","w":500,"h":666,"by":"Jennifer","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AngelFoodCake.jpg"}},"ingredient/sweetener":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/sweetener","n":"Sweetener","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["A sweetener is a substance added to food or drink to impart the flavor of sweetness, either because it contains a type of sugar, or because it contains a sweet-tasting sugar substitute. Various natural non-sugar sweeteners  (NSS) and artificial sweeteners are used to produce food and drink."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sweetener"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweetener"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Ukrainian cuisine","cuisine/ukrainian-cuisine",[["Candy","dish/candy"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Honey","ingredient/honey"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]}]},"ingredient/pernil":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/pernil","n":"Pernil","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Pernil (pernil asado, pernil al horno, roast pork) is a slow-roasted marinated pork leg or pork shoulder common in Puerto Rico, Dominican Republic, Cuba, Colombia, Venezuela and Ecuador. Pernil is typically accompanied by rice and is commonly shared during Christmas."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-pernil"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pernil"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Bolivian cuisine","cuisine/bolivian-cuisine",[["Chola sandwich","dish/chola-sandwich"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Escabeche","ingredient/escabeche"],["Torresmo","ingredient/torresmo"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/5/56/Pernil.1.jpg/500px-Pernil.1.jpg","w":500,"h":321,"by":"Ekem","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pernil.1.jpg"}},"dish/dapanji":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/dapanji","n":"Dapanji","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Chinese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Dapanji is a spicy chicken stew that was invented by a Han Chinese chef in Shawan, Xinjiang in the 1980s. Although originally considered Chinese rather than Uyghur, the chef made the dish halal to accommodate local religious customs, and it quickly became popular among the local Uyghur population."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-dapanji"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dapanji"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Woks of Life","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thewoksoflife.com","note":"Chinese and Chinese American recipes from the Leung family, running since 2013.","url":"https://thewoksoflife.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Chinese Cooking Demystified","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"youtube.com","note":"Technique-heavy YouTube channel on regional Chinese home an