"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-saikan"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saikan"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Buddhist cuisine","cuisine/buddhist-cuisine"],["Chinese Buddhist cuisine","cuisine/chinese-buddhist-cuisine"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/b/b3/Saikan1.jpg/500px-Saikan1.jpg","w":500,"h":335,"by":"Rei at en.wikipedia","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saikan1.jpg"}},"dish/sel-roti":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/sel-roti","n":"Sel roti","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Nepalese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Sel roti is a traditional Nepalese ring-shaped sweet fried dough made from rice flour. It is mostly prepared during Dashain and Tihar, widely celebrated Hindu festivals in Nepal as well as Darjeeling, Kalimpong and Sikkim and the Kumaon region of Uttarakhand. The dish is popular throughout Nepal. Sel roti is made from a batter of rice flour, water, sugar, ghee, and spices which is then deep-fried in cooking oil."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-sel-roti"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sel_roti"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Nepalese cuisine","cuisine/nepalese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Ghee","ingredient/ghee"],["Rice flour","ingredient/rice-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Gundruk","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thegundruk.com","note":"Blog dedicated to Nepali recipes and food culture.","url":"https://thegundruk.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Nepalese cuisine","links":[["Dhikri","dish/dhikri"],["Ghonghi","dish/ghonghi"],["Mokthuk","dish/mokthuk"],["Momo (food)","dish/momo-food"],["Sohari","dish/sohari"],["Thali","dish/thali"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/c/c0/Sel_Roti.jpg/500px-Sel_Roti.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Swapnet at English Wikipedia","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sel_Roti.jpg"}},"dish/spaghetti":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/spaghetti","n":"Spaghetti","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Spaghetti is a long, thin, solid, cylindrical pasta. It serves as a staple food of Italian cuisine and is made of milled wheat and water (sometimes enriched with vitamins and minerals), with the standard Italian version using durum-wheat semolina. The pasta is usually white because refined flour is used, but whole wheat flour may be added. Spaghettoni is a thicker form of spaghetti, while spaghettini is a thinner form. Capellini is a very thin spaghetti, while vermicelli is intermediate."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-spaghetti"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spaghetti"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"Vicky Bennison's long-running video series filming Italian grandmothers making regional pasta by hand.","url":"https://pastagrannies.substack.com/p/pasta-grannies-is-now-on-substack","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Recipes from Italy","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"recipesfromitaly.com","note":"Traditional Italian recipes written by Italian home cooks, organized by region and course.","url":"https://recipesfromitaly.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Manu's Menu","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"manusmenu.com","note":"Italian-born home cook Manuela sharing classic family and regional Italian dishes.","url":"https://www.manusmenu.com/about/about-this-site","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Italian cuisine","links":[["Acquacotta","dish/acquacotta"],["Agliata","dish/agliata"],["Agnolotti","dish/agnolotti"],["Antipasto","dish/antipasto"],["Arancini","dish/arancini"],["Biscotti","dish/biscotti"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Bombolone","dish/bombolone"],["Budino","dish/budino"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Cannelloni","dish/cannelloni"],["Capellini","dish/capellini"],["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Carpaccio","dish/carpaccio"],["Cassatella di sant'Agata","dish/cassatella-di-sant-agata"],["Cassoeula","dish/cassoeula"],["Ciabatta","dish/ciabatta"],["Cioppino","dish/cioppino"],["Coda alla vaccinara","dish/coda-alla-vaccinara"],["Colomba pasquale","dish/colomba-pasquale"],["Conti roll","dish/conti-roll"],["Cotoletta alla bolognese","dish/cotoletta-alla-bolognese"],["Crostata","dish/crostata"],["Drago restaurants","dish/drago-restaurants"],["Focaccia pugliese","dish/focaccia-pugliese"],["Frittata","dish/frittata"],["Giardiniera","dish/giardiniera"],["Guanciale","dish/guanciale"],["Italian restaurant","dish/italian-restaurant"],["Italian wedding soup","dish/italian-wedding-soup"],["Lampredotto","dish/lampredotto"],["Lasagna","dish/lasagna"],["List of Italian restaurants","dish/list-of-italian-restaurants"],["Marinara sauce","dish/marinara-sauce"],["Mondeghili","dish/mondeghili"],["Paccheri","dish/paccheri"],["Panini (sandwich)","dish/panini-sandwich"],["Panna cotta","dish/panna-cotta"],["Passatelli","dish/passatelli"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/4/48/Pasta_%2823727887804%29.jpg/500px-Pasta_%2823727887804%29.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Tim Reckmann from Hamm, Deutschland","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pasta_(23727887804).jpg"}},"ingredient/saguaro":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/saguaro","n":"Saguaro fruit","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 0 dishes across 0 cuisines","intro":[["Bahidaj, the fruit of the saguaro cactus, is gathered by the ",["Tohono O'odham","cuisine/tohono-o-odham-foodways"]," in midsummer with long poles made from saguaro ribs. The harvest opens the O'odham new year, and the pulp is cooked into syrup, jam and wine."]],"src":"note","sources":[{"name":"Tucson Spotlight and O'odham Media, Saguaro fruit harvest sustains Tohono O'odham traditions","url":"https://www.tucsonspotlight.org/saguaro-fruit-harvest-sustains-tohono-oodham-traditions/"}],"actions":[{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saguaro"}],"sections":[{"h":"Mentioned in","links":[["Tohono O'odham foodways","cuisine/tohono-o-odham-foodways"]]}]}}